  "regression_evidence": [
    "Invalid/trailing phase bytes are rejected; legacy snapshots default to unknown and diagnostic wording no longer controls first-prompt presentation.",
    "Legacy, link-only and phase-capable attachment paths preserve capabilities without relaunch on negotiation retry.",
    "A blocked old descriptor writer finishes after connection destruction and replacement; the newest descriptor survives and no temporary remains.",
    "An unwritable registry keeps its original bytes and starts no missing service. This strengthens ordering without claiming a reproduced prior orphan.",
    "The initial offscreen window-state failure was a synthetic two-pixel frame shift. Disabling synthetic margins passes the unchanged native geometry implementation."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Native macOS keyboard/pointer/IME, pasteboard, external URL handlers and GPU presentation were not requalified.",
    "TSan excludes the pre-existing uninstrumented Qt handoff report in asynchronous harness-model work; no whole-desktop race clearance is claimed.",
    "Descriptor ticket ordering is same-process; no cross-process writer lock is claimed.",
    "Old service binaries cannot supply OSC 8 metadata or read newly extended history archives; see terminal-usability.json.",
    "Q09 deterministic deferred-history regression, Q10 allocation measurement and Q13 shared wire fixture remain separate follow-up. No new milestone features were built.",
    "Running user apps/services and unrelated dirty worktrees were preserved."
  ],
